    <statement><p>Find the least common denominator (LCD) of the rational expressions:  
<me>\frac{2y}{y^{2}-25} \mbox{ and } \frac{4}{y^{2}-5y}</me></p>
<p>LCD:  <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y\mathopen{}\left(y-5\right)\mathopen{}\left(y+5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The factors of the denominators are</p>
<p><m>y^{2}-25 = \left(y-5\right)\mathopen{}\left(y+5\right)</m></p>
<p><m>y^{2}-5y = y\mathopen{}\left(y-5\right)</m></p>
<p>Hence, the LCD is <m>y\mathopen{}\left(y-5\right)\mathopen{}\left(y+5\right)</m>.</p>
</solution>
